cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite or reference the AI Governance Standards Baseline dataset, please cite Dr Michelle O'Rourke and CAM Initiative. Public availability does not grant permission to reproduce, adapt, derive from, or otherwise reuse original VIGIL material; see LICENSE.md. Third-party sources remain subject to their own rights."
title: "AI Governance Standards Baseline"
type: dataset
version: "0.0.1"
date-released: "2026-08-24"
authors:
  - family-names: "O'Rourke"
    given-names: "Michelle"
    name-particle: "Dr"
abstract: >
  The AI Governance Standards Baseline is a machine-readable VIGIL Observatory
  dataset of governance-source metadata and clause/control records drawn from
  laws, standards, frameworks and technical guidance relevant to AI governance.
  It provides source-level public summaries, AI-governance relevance themes,
  lifecycle applicability, substantive review dates and clause-level analytical
  requirement records where available.
keywords:
  - "AI governance"
  - "AI standards"
  - "AI regulation"
  - "governance requirements"
  - "assurance"
  - "risk management"
  - "VIGIL Observatory"
  - "VIGIL"
repository-code: "https://github.com/CAM-Initiative/Vigil"
url: "https://www.cam-initiative.org/observatory/knowledge-base/standards-sources"
identifiers:
  - type: "url"
    value: "https://github.com/CAM-Initiative/Vigil/tree/main/vigil/external_governance/requirements"
notes: >
  Dataset version 0.0.1. Review-freshness-only updates may regenerate package
  artefacts without incrementing the semantic dataset version; package build
  metadata and integrity hashes are recorded in the accompanying manifest.
